 "extract": "The buff-breasted sandpiper (Calidris subruficollis) is a small shorebird. The species name subruficollis is from Latin subrufus, \"reddish\" (from sub, \"somewhat\", and rufus, \"rufous\") and collis, \"-necked/-throated\" (from collum, \"neck\"). It is a calidrid sandpiper, notable for its long annual migration, from the artic region of North America to the pampas region of South America.",
